# Mechanism: pre-release-arithmetic-boundaries

command: python3 -B scripts/check-pre-release-arithmetic-boundaries.py
inputs:
  - .cairn/mechanisms/pre-release-arithmetic-boundaries
  - Cargo.toml
  - Cargo.lock
  - src/display/adaptive.rs
  - src/display/capabilities.rs
  - src/display/monitor.rs
  - src/layout/grid.rs
  - tests/arithmetic_boundaries.rs
  - scripts/check-pre-release-arithmetic-boundaries.py
requirements:
  - RTR-004

The check MUST first prove its process validator rejects a timeout, a failed
process, and missing completion. It MUST then exercise the public adaptive FPS
manager with zero, equal, ordered, and reversed bounds. Every constructed
manager and every manual target MUST retain a nonzero target and frame duration.

The check MUST also exercise the public automatic grid with zero columns across
multiple row and item counts. Zero-column input MUST return a grid with no
placed children and MUST NOT panic. Both API groups MUST report explicit
completion within the test deadline.
